id: pm-starter-gx6x
title: Canonicalize the starter workspace read and adopt the current pm host contract
description: "pm-starter still shells out through deprecated list-all and legacy --include-body forms, its raw manifest retains an ignored pm.compatibility object, its exact development CLI/SDK is 2026.8.15 while the installed and published host is 2026.8.21, and every changelog read except one is bounded or may resolve a non-project host. Migrate the reference package to canonical complete reads without weakening its strict whole-workspace refusal."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[5]: agent-ux,compatibility,completeness,latest-cli,tdd
created_at: "2026-08-21T04:35:12.408Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T04:49:19.002Z"
assignee: codex
claim_principal: codex
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: Create red-first tests for canonical pm list --all argv with output-include full plus unbounded budget and limit; preserve strict pagination omission count duplicate and unusable-row refusal; remove only unsupported manifest metadata and validate the complete raw manifest through the public SDK; exact-pin development to pm 2026.8.21 while keeping the minimum behavior floor justified; route all package and release-workflow changelog reads through the project CLI with both output bounds disabled; update dependencies to their latest compatible published versions; run the full existing release gate and report its literal coverage dimensions without calling three dimensions four; prove packed npm and Bun behavior on a fresh real tracker with empty deprecation stderr; track the separate exact four-dimensional quality work in pm-starter-qu97; do not merge or publish while pm-starter-asud remains open
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: pm-starter main 714da9a; installed and npm-latest pm CLI/SDK 2026.8.21; npm pm-starter 2026.8.17
repro_steps: Run the demo workspace reader under pm 2026.8.21 and observe the list-all deprecation diagnostic; run pm health --strict-exit against the stale project extension; pass complete manifest.json to checkExtensionManifestCompatibility; inspect package and release changelog argv.
resolution: Migrated the reference reader and release plumbing to the canonical pm 2026.8.21 contract without weakening fail-closed completeness checks or overstating the repository quality gate.
expected_result: The starter reference exercises the latest CLI/SDK through canonical complete and unbounded contracts with zero manifest findings and deprecation-free npm/Bun acceptance.
actual_result: "Canonical complete-corpus reader, current host/dependencies, zero-finding raw manifest, unbounded local changelog reads, exact three-dimensional measured coverage, and fresh packed npm/Bun behavior pass. Strict doctor has one upstream-only safe-decline limitation tracked as pm-cli#1074; independent history/privacy and four-dimensional quality blockers remain open."
component: starter host integration and release plumbing
customer_impact: "Agents copy pm-starter as the canonical extension reference, so stale aliases and host contracts propagate deprecation noise and unsafe bounded reads into newly scaffolded packages."
